<title>SINGAPORE: South Korea's refinery turnarounds start - table.</title>
<headline>South Korea's refinery turnarounds start - table.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>LG-Caltex Oil Corp, a unit of the LG Group  LUGG.CN will kick off South Korea's refinery turnaround season when it shuts one of its four crude distillation units (CDU) on Tuesday.</p>
<p>All five South Korean refiners are scheduled to carry out maintenance shutdowns this year, lasting until October.</p>
<p>The details of the 1997 turnarounds are as follows:</p>
<p>(capacity is in barrels per day)</p>
<p>UNIT				    CAPACITY    SHUTDOWN PERIOD</p>
<p>YUKONG LTD</p>
<p>CDU 3				    170,000    Aug 7-Sept 7</p>
<p>mid-dist desulphuriser		50,000</p>
<p>CDU 5				    200,000    Jun 2-Jul 9</p>
<p>Desulphuriser			   60,000</p>
<p>Mid-dist desulphurisers		7,000    May 6-16</p>
<p>					    15,000    May 22-Jun 5</p>
<p>					    45,000    Sept 22-Oct 14</p>
<p>hydrocracker			    30,000    May 23-Jun 24</p>
<p>vacuum residue desulphuriser	30,000    May 21-Jun 20</p>
<p>residue fluid catalytic cracker   50,000    Jul 26-Sept 3</p>
<p>residue hydro desulphuriser	 60,000    Jul 21-Sept 4</p>
<p>CDU 1				    100,000    Jun 1-14</p>
<p>CDU 2				    130,000    Apr 15-May 15</p>
<p>CDU 3				    150,000    Jun 9-18</p>
<p>CDU 4				    220,000    Jul 16-Aug 29</p>
<p>HANWHA ENERGY CO</p>
<p>CDU 1				     75,000    Sep 21-Oct 23</p>
